Identify and document the current bucket configuration including region, size, object count, versioning, and IAM access.
Create a temporary S3 bucket (niwas-bucket-temp) in the Mobicule AWS account in the same region with versioning and encryption enabled.
Configure secure cross-account IAM access to allow the Mobicule account to read data from the Niwas bucket.
Perform an initial full data sync from the Niwas bucket to the temporary Mobicule bucket without impacting production.
Validate the sync by comparing object count, total size, and random file integrity checks.
Schedule a short maintenance window for final cutover.
Stop all cron jobs and application uploads to prevent new writes during migration.
Perform a final delta sync to ensure no data loss.
Delete the original bucket from the Niwas AWS account.
Immediately recreate the same bucket name in the Mobicule AWS account in the same region.
Restore all data from the temporary bucket to the newly created final bucket.
Update IAM roles and remove old cross-account access configurations.
Restart cron jobs and resume application operations.
Monitor the system for 24–48 hours to confirm stability.
Delete the temporary bucket and proceed with Niwas AWS account decommissioning after validation.
